{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the land which you, etc.</b> It is difficult: after he said in the preceding verse ״כִּי הָאָרֶץ״ etc., what place is there to go back and say ״וְהָאָרֶץ״, since that statement is the conclusion of the matters he began to speak in the preceding verse? And it appears that the delineation of the verse is as follows: for at first he mentioned the praise of the land in his saying <b>a land flowing with milk and honey</b>, and he concluded by saying <b>for the land</b> etc. <b>is not like the land of Egypt</b> etc. — meaning, even though the land of Egypt is praiseworthy for its fruits, as it is written ״כְּגַן ה׳ כְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם״ (Genesis 13:10), still, not by this measure alone is the land that HaShem gives. And further, there is a deficiency in the land of Egypt: <b>which you sow</b> etc. <b>and you water</b> etc., and he concluded by saying <b>but the land which you</b> etc. <b>drinks water from the rain of heaven</b> etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:30.510932595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}